# Cloudflare Pages _redirects
# Format: <source> <destination> <status>
# Trailing "!" forces the redirect even if a matching file exists.

# www → apex (301 permanent)
# Requires `www.pymewebpro.com` to be attached to this Pages project as a
# custom domain (Pages → Custom domains → Add www.pymewebpro.com). Without
# that binding Pages never sees the request and this rule has no effect —
# in that case configure a Cloudflare zone-level Redirect Rule instead.
https://www.pymewebpro.com/*  https://pymewebpro.com/:splat  301!
http://www.pymewebpro.com/*   https://pymewebpro.com/:splat  301!

# /en/ is a real path again — English translation lives there.
# (Earlier we 301'd /en/* → / during the LATAM-only commit; reversed
# now that we're shipping a real English version.)

# Legacy /es/ paths -> apex (Spanish is the default at / since LATAM-only
# pivot). The whole site is Spanish at apex, so /es/ prefix is meaningless.
/es/*   /:splat   301
/es     /         301

# /privacy (old English PIPEDA / Quebec Law 25 policy) retired · send old links to the Colombian data policy
/privacy        /politica-de-datos   301!
/privacy.html   /politica-de-datos   301!

# /hosting (legacy $30.000/mes hosting-renewal page) retired 2026-06-01 · hosting is
# now bundled into the $150.000/mes Plan mensual. Forced 301 to home (301! keeps the
# old hosting.html file unreachable without editing it, so no CSP hash churn).
/hosting        /   301!
/hosting.html   /   301!

# Note: Cloudflare Pages automatically serves *.html files at the extension-less
# URL and 308-redirects /name.html → /name. So /hosting.html, /terminos.html,
# /politica-de-datos.html, /privacy.html all resolve at the extension-less path.
# All canonical URLs and sitemap entries use the extension-less form.

# Mockups gallery moved to the mockups.pymewebpro.com subdomain (served by the
# portal worker, which proxies the demo files from /manual-mockups/<slug>/ below).
# IMPORTANT: only the bare gallery root bounces. Do NOT add a /manual-mockups/*
# splat rule: the worker proxy fetches /manual-mockups/<slug>/... from this apex,
# so a splat redirect would loop the proxy. The <slug> subpaths stay served.
/manual-mockups   https://mockups.pymewebpro.com/   301!
/manual-mockups/  https://mockups.pymewebpro.com/   301!
